    <p class="dek" style="margin-top:1rem"><strong>Every name in the table above is a link now, and
    on 22 September it was not.</strong> Publication was <strong>Hedviga's blood</strong>, so Anka
    Blažević's children had pages while <strong>Martin, the elder Antun and Pavao</strong> — who
    married into the family or fathered into it — had none, even though this archive had read more
    documents for Pavao and Martin than for most people who did.
    <strong>The rule gained two more doors that day.</strong> <em>A person this archive has opened a
    page for gets a page</em>, listed in <span class="mono">sources/documented.psv</span>; and
    <strong>the parents of every published person, to the root</strong>, because a page that says
